menu "Attachments: one brain, many radios (ATTACHMENT-DESIGN)"

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_CODEC
	bool
	default y if MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN || MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD || MESHTASTIC_RELAY_EAR
	help
	  The envelope a radio head and its brain exchange (pure byte packing).
	  Pulled in by anything that speaks it; not a user choice.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACH_BEARER
	bool
	default y if MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_CODEC
	help
	  The board-to-board link behind the attachments (ATTACHMENT-SCOPE §4):
	  a registry of bearers -- the BLE peer link, a wire, a test pipe -- each
	  a send and a link_info. Envelopes never see a bearer's types.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	bool "This node is a brain: it hears through radio heads"
	default n
	help
	  Accept attachment envelopes over the BLE peer link. A head's RX_FRAME
	  enters the router as an RF frame tagged with the head's preset and
	  signal; the node's identity, keys, NodeDB and modules stay exactly as
	  they are. Costs a small table (MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_MAX entries) and
	  8 B per RX queue slot; the code is flash.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_MAX
	int "Radio heads a brain tracks (its own radio is not counted)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	default 4
	range 1 8
	help
	  A BLE peer link per head; the R8 has 3 connection slots in total.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_EVICT_SEC
	int "Seconds a head stays in the table after its link went down"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	default 180
	range 1 3600
	help
	  A head whose bearer link dropped keeps its slot (and counters) this long
	  so a reboot or a BLE hiccup re-admits it in place; after that the slot
	  is freed. A head that speaks again before then is simply up again.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_ALLOW_MAX
	int "Operator allow-list entries (heads admitted on an untrusted link)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	default 4
	range 1 8

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	bool "This node is a keyless radio head"
	depends on !MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_BRAIN
	default n
	help
	  The radio forwards every frame it hears, undecoded, with its RSSI/SNR
	  and preset, to its brain over the peer link (overlay-ble-peer.conf; on
	  native_sim the send is a test seam), and retunes when the brain says
	  so. Transmit for the brain is phase 3. The image carries no channel
	  keys, no PKI, no NodeDB and no config beyond its preset and its brain:
	  build with samples/meshtastic/overlay-attachment-head.conf, whose
	  post-build step refuses an image in which any of those linked
	  (cmake/keyless-assert.cmake). The router is never reached from the
	  radio on a head; origination is refused at the outbound queue.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD_BRAIN_ID
	hex "The brain's node number (0 = set at runtime)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	default 0
	help
	  Baked-in brain. `meshtastic attach brain <id>` overrides it and the
	  value persists (mtattach/brain) with MESHTASTIC_SETTINGS.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD_STATUS_PERIOD_SEC
	int "STATUS report period (s)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	default 60
	range 5 3600

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD_TX_QUEUE_SIZE
	int "Frames the brain has handed this head, waiting to key up"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	default 4
	range 1 16
	help
	  TX_FRAMEs accepted from the brain and not yet transmitted. A full queue
	  refuses the envelope (counted; the brain sees no TX_RESULT). Each entry
	  is a full airframe.

config MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD_QUEUE_SIZE
	int "Frames queued for the brain"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_ATTACHMENT_HEAD
	default 4
	range 1 16
	help
	  Between the RX thread and the forwarding work item. ~260 B each.

endmenu
